    "parsed": {
      "report_date": "2026-11-20",
      "title": "Inside the ‘Party’ Panel: How Fraudsters Rent Android Banking Trojans to Target Indian Bank Customers",
      "summary": "A rent-a-trojan service, uncovered by CloudSEK's XVigil platform, lets fraudsters build fake Google Play pages and branded Android banking malware targeting Indian bank and card customers. A fake credit-card app page collects card number, expiry, CVV, date of birth and mother's name before pushing a sideloaded APK. The APK is a dropper that installs a hidden SMS stealer, which forwards bank OTPs and sets call forwarding so verification calls reach the attacker. An unprotected panel server exposed 50 tenant accounts, 34 of them paid, targeting six Indian banks and card issuers as well as government-service users. Defenders should warn customers to install apps only from official stores and monitor for unexpected call-forwarding activation around card-not-present transactions.",
      "completeness": "Medium",
      "threats": [
        "Sms_stealer"
      ],
