      "title": "MoldyRoost: A Malvertising Machine Built to Deliver iOS Exploits",
      "summary": "MoldyRoost is a large malvertising operation that buys programmatic ads and uses cloaked landing pages to deliver iOS exploit chains, with no user action needed beyond loading the page. It uses existing exploit kits, Coruna and DarkSword, and picks one for each visitor by iOS version, while the operation itself adds the ad-based distribution. Its payloads are built to steal crypto wallet seed phrases, keychain data, messages and photos. Its ads have targeted more than 47 countries, with the largest share aimed at Hong Kong. The report assesses that the six sub-clusters form one operation, and a leaked source repository showed per-channel tracking of stolen data.",
