      "title": "BabidiGhost: An AI-Augmented Cybercrime Operation",
      "summary": "BabidiGhost is a French-speaking, low-skill operator who used a jailbroken AI agent from the BlackHatSect0r toolchain to target European banks, insurers, payment providers and municipalities over nine days in November 2026. The agent wrote the scanners, exploits and exfiltration scripts while the operator typed plain-language orders. Successful intrusions relied only on known weaknesses, including an unpatched analytics tool, a readable database credential, a weak administrator password and unauthenticated API endpoints. Ordinary controls such as MFA, IP allowlisting and server-side validation stopped the agent wherever they were in place. The model API key was revoked on November 14, 2026, but already-deployed implants kept checking in for about another day.",
