    "parsed": {
      "report_date": "2026-11-20",
      "title": "ARTEX in the Tenant: How an Agentic Offensive Framework Abused an Entra Application to Mint Disposable Accounts",
      "summary": "An operator abused an existing Microsoft Entra application in a US financial-services tenant in October 2026, using it to create three user accounts and obtain tokens for an internal business API. Each account was given a password at creation, signed in within seconds using the resource owner password credentials grant, and was disabled about five minutes later. The application also held the Exchange Online full_access_as_app role, which grants mailbox access across the tenant, though no mailbox access was observed. Abnormal Intelligence links the activity to ARTEX and AntiFox with moderate confidence, based on shared infrastructure rather than proven framework execution. Defenders should treat the compromised application itself as the durable risk: revoke its credentials and roles, review every account it created, and alert on sequences of service-principal user creation, password-grant sign-in, and disabling.",
