      "title": "ROMULUS ClickFix to LegionLoader and Warden Stealer: Breaking Down a Multi-Stage Malware Intrusion",
      "summary": "eSentire's Threat Response Unit observed a multi-stage intrusion using ROMULUS, a ClickFix delivery system, which led to LegionLoader and ultimately Warden Stealer. The victim was tricked into pasting a clipboard command that downloaded and ran a malicious MSI file. The MSI decrypted embedded PowerShell and C# stages, which launched shellcode that checked for sandboxes and virtual machines before reflectively loading LegionLoader. LegionLoader registered with its C2 server, then downloaded Warden Loader and injected it into ilasm.exe via process hollowing. Defenders are advised to disable the Windows Run prompt via Group Policy, run phishing awareness training, and deploy NGAV or EDR at minimum.",
