      "title": "Inside a Gentlemen Ransomware-Linked Intrusion",
      "summary": "A deception alert triggered by scanning of decoy backup infrastructure exposed a multi-week intrusion linked to Gentlemen ransomware. The threat actor used valid credentials, previously exposed in a stealer log, to sign in through an internet-facing Citrix VDI environment that lacked multifactor authentication. Once inside, the operator mapped Active Directory, performed large-scale account enumeration, and opened files containing plaintext passwords and tokens. The intrusion escalated to domain-level control by re-enabling a disabled Domain Admin account and adding a service identity to Domain Admins, with SFTP activity observed to external addresses. Defenders should enforce phishing-resistant MFA on remote access paths, investigate stealer-log exposures, and remove plaintext secrets from shares.",
