    "parsed": {
      "report_date": "2026-11-20",
      "title": "One VHDX kit, five lures: ChatGPT-signed decoys on euro policy and Moldovan finance",
      "summary": "A VHDX-based spear-phishing kit, active since at least September 2026, delivers document lures in ZIP archives that mount as virtual disks containing a Windows shortcut disguised as a PDF. Clicking it runs a hidden command prompt that launches a real-looking decoy PDF and a small downloader, which checks reachability to reddit[.]com, bing.com or wikipedia.org before fetching a command from a fresh .top domain. The five builds examined share the same compiled code, with lures impersonating a euro-policy event, the National Bank of Moldova, Ministry of Finance and a tax-reporting procedure. Two decoys carry C2PA Content Credentials showing they were generated by ChatGPT. The server address is XOR-scrambled with a GUID passed on the command line, so it isn't visible in plain text. Defenders should alert on conhost.exe --headless launching cmd.exe, hunt for the fake PowerShell User-Agent, and treat disk-image \"documents\" with suspicion.",
